{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486773-messy-crits-severity","id":1486773,"title":"Messy crits severity.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-17T08:58:27-07:00","id":1486773,"title":"Messy crits severity.","content":"So, I have been asked to run a V5 one shot and I'm trying to figure out a way to not make messy crits a bother like they usually turn out in game, one Idea I had is to make the consequences severity dependant on the character's actual hunger level, for example, say a witness comes on you after you just trespassed somewhere, you want to stop them from calling the police:<br /> <br /> 1) If you have hunger 1 and roll a crit then you will stop them but do so in a way that will definitely leave an impression like snatching their phone and crushing it in your hand while giving them the mother of all death stares, this might make it easier to identify you at a later time but is otherwise not an issue in the immediate future.<br /> <br /> 2) If you have hunger 2 you still don't kill them but will end up roughing them up a little more than necessary, say knocking them down and kicking them a few times to make sure they stay down, this will draw more heat from the police and might increase police attention in the area after but for the moment, you are good.<br /> <br /> 3) If you have hunger 3 things will start to get messy, you savagely beat them, maybe putting them in critical condition, you will definitely attract a lot more heat after this and the police will become a more stable presence in the chronicle for a while, maybe you could get a stain depending on your convictions, for the task at hand you might have attracked more attention from other people on the scene depending on how much of a ruckus you made.<br /> <br /> 4) If you have hunger 4 than you kill them, it will most likely be unintentional like grabbing them by the throat to stop them from screaming and crashing their larynx or beat them too hard and cause fatal injuries, you are in the shit now, you just left a dead body and turned what might have been a minor effraction into an homicide, it will make the news and cops will be onto you, patroling the streets and making your other tasks (including hunting) more difficult, oh and you definitely get a stain for this.<br /> <br /> 5) If you have hunger 5 than congrats, you just butchered the poor sod in a way that is unlikely even for the most rabid animal, this will make national news and attract the SI attention, making the rest of the chronicle a living hell for your character unless they manage the unlikely feat of covering this up in some way, the character is definitely going to take more than one stain but that might not even matter since the masquerade violation will definitely attract the sheriff attention thus making your unlife expectancy considerably shorter...<br /> <br /> I have used a more &quot;hands on&quot; example because they are usually the ones that create more problems (at least in my experience), messy crits in social situations will be much easier to handle since it will mostly consist of leaving the wrong kind of impression and drawing more attention than necessary, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}